# ── Teddy-foundation — what never belongs in the repository ──────────────────────────
# Everything listed here is created by the app on first run. A fresh clone with
# none of it present boots straight to the setup screen, which is the intended
# first experience — so nothing here needs to be committed, and some of it must
# never be.

# ── Secrets. Committing any of these publishes them. ──────────────────────────
#
# Every comment here is on its OWN line, and that is not a style preference.
# In a .gitignore, "#" only starts a comment at the START of a line: a trailing
# "# explanation" is part of the pattern. These five entries each carried one,
# so each matched a filename ending in its own explanatory text — that is to
# say, nothing. `git check-ignore config/api_keys.json` reported it unprotected.
# The comments written to explain why these files must never be committed were
# the reason they were not protected from being committed.

# your Gemini API key, plus per-plugin credentials
config/api_keys.json
# the dashboard's TLS private key and certificate
config/certs/
# a LINKED WhatsApp session — committing it hands somebody your WhatsApp
# account, not just a key
config/whatsapp_web/
# Google OAuth tokens (Gmail / Calendar plugins)
**/token*.json
# Google OAuth client secrets
**/client_secret*.json
# the Android client's device credential (server/auth.py)
*credentials*.json
.env
.env.*

# ── Personal data the assistant accumulates about you ─────────────────────────
memory/long_term.json
memory/*.db

# ── Python build noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# ── Virtual environments ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# ── Editors and operating systems ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ── Runtime output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
logs/
downloads/
screenshots/

# ── jarvis-preprod : ce qu'une campagne produit ───────────────────────────────
#
# reports/latest est effacé au début de chaque campagne (fresh_reports), et
# server.pid désigne un processus qui n'existe plus sur une autre machine.
# Le laboratoire est du source ; ses verdicts, ses captures et ses logcat sont
# des observations datées, qui se rejouent au lieu de se versionner.
jarvis-preprod/reports/
